WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.190
I see.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.870
So Maruruha has fallen?

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.630
The Uzuurussha forces have crossed the border, I'm told,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.760
and invaded Yamato.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.970
It is not Yamato who shall rule this land,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.510
but we, the Uzuurussha!

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.020
Foolish barbarians... They would attack Yamato?

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.270
Ye starving wolves, sink your fangs into Yamato's neck!

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:33.030
Let those who would dare commit the sin of transgression face our punishment!

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.500
Cleaning the ditches day after day...

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:18.860
With Oshutoru gone, I thought I wouldn't have to do this anymore.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.510
They've been ordered to join the assault?

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.420
Now that the war against the Uzuurussha has begun,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.820
all the Ouros that rule over the various lands of Yamato are being dispatched.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.950
But Atui's father is Soyankekuru-sama, the Ouro of Shahhoro,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.420
and Rurutie's father is Oozen, the Ouro of Kujuuri.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.340
Neither are currently able to leave their land,

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.290
so they're sending Atui and Rurutie in their stead.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.340
They'll be meeting up with Oshutoru, but...

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.290
Just the two of them going alone has me worried.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.300
I'm going to follow them with Nosuri.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.050
So if you wouldn't mind...

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.740
I'd really like you to come with us, Haku.{suddenly Kuon route}

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.940
You're really good to have around.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.430
Will you?

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.460
Uh, sure...

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.520
Really? Thank you!

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.260
Retreat! Retreat!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.600
Reporting!

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.850
We have destroyed the enemy army, and they are in full retreat!

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:00.350
Dekoponpo-sama, that was truly splendid commanding.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.360
Excellent. Excellent.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.350
We're saved...

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.850
We should retreat for now and prepare for the next phase.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.870
Retreat and prepare?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.850
What are you talking about?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.880
This is a golden opportunity.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.380
Now's the time to annihilate those barbarians who defy Yamato,

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:26.130
and show those insolent fools the true power of Dekoponpo-sama!

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:27.510
Bokoinante!

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.220
Order all forces to pursue!

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.930
Understood!

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.170
Please wait!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.710
If we pursue them further—

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.370
Shut up!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.900
Let none escape!

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.650
Dekoponpo-sama has given his orders!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.070
We will end this war here!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.480
They fell for it.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.670
Reporting!

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.760
The enemy ambushed us!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.230
They had forces waiting in the mountains!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.210
Wh-What?

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.680
I knew it!

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:17.790
That area is ideal for hiding troops for an ambush!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.440
Why didn't you say that earlier, Maroro!?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.470
I tried to, but you wouldn't let me!

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.990
What should we do?

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.500
Let me see...

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.080
I did have another unit in that area.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.330
You mustn't mobilize that unit!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.580
Silence!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.740
Send reinforcements immediately!

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.250
Yes, sir!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.340
Th-This is bad...

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.050
Master Haku...

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:59.480
I didn't think I'd end up going to war, too.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.580
Well, if we can just get to Oshutoru,

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:08.210
I can stop cleaning ditches. That's a plus.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.200
Alas, Kuon!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.950
Victory is mine for the taking!

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.490
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.750
Don't whine about this later!

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:21.310
Here I go!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.690
Five, huh?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.720
One, two, three...

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.670
Should I take out this piece, or go two spaces ahead and take out that piece?

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.890
I'll take this one!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.450
Sorry, wrong one.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.960
That was a decoy.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.900
I believe this is the one you wanted.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.400
Checkmate!

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.010
Kuon-han wins!

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.680
Wait! My hand slipped!

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.650
I actually wanted to take out <i>this</i> one!

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.280
A good woman never asks for do-overs.{shouldn't be a sore loser.]{orig: A good woman doesn't ask for backsies.}{matta (lit. wait) is a thing in shogi where you can fix your move, usually has a limit and is only used in casual games}

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.700
Sister.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.840
Kuon-han, you ain't bad at games either.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.830
Yes, my mothers enjoyed them.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:12.280
I really improved by playing against them.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:15.050
It's Rurutie's turn next.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.070
I...

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.100
Come on, it's mighty fun.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.440
R-Right...

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.980
In that case, I'll play!

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.950
It's time for me to show you my true capabilities!

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:41.830
How's things?

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.340
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.380
Yeah?

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.590
Anyway, should we all be this relaxed?

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.910
I mean, we're going to war.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.090
This feels more like a vacation.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.590
I want Rurutie to cheer up.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.940
Even if she's doing it for her country,

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.850
this is still her first battle.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.120
I'm sure she's nervous.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.560
Checkmate. Guess I win!

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.730
You doubled your winnings again!

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:12.460
Looks like someone else is getting cheered up instead.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.440
Yeah.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:18.970
Huh?

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.130
We came out of the forest, 
and there was the battlefield!

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:35.470
But now's no time for talking!

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.010
Hey, Haku!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:54.570
Okay, we should be safe now.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.990
What in heaven's name was that?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.360
There's a war going on! A war!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.100
There were all these arrows flying at us.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.910
If we got caught up in that, 
there's no way we'd survive.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.450
We're leaving.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.020
What are you doing?

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.620
Hurry up and get in.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.210
We're leaving now.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.760
But mister, we came here to fight a war in the first place.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:20.080
We've done enough.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.170
Doing any more would be insane.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.650
You still want to fight?

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.640
Of course!

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.870
We came here for that sole reason!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.900
To fight for our country!

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.530
I gotta do my best and make my pa proud!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:40.920
But getting hit by an arrow hurts like hell!

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.750
We're aware.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.790
Y-You're really going to fight?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.820
That crest...

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.820
Those must be Oshutoru's men.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.830
But I don't see Oshutoru anywhere.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:29.130
Maybe he left them to handle this and went further ahead?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.950
He said something about saving that Doeboiponpo guy.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:34.090
Maybe.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:37.020
Then let's go on ahead ourselves.

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:42.470
Our mission is to meet up with the Generals of the Right and Left, right?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.620
I can't believe the Uzuurussha fight without armor.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.220
Do they have a death wish?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.590
Now that you mention it...

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.980
But them people standin' near the back are wearin' armor.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.620
They might be Nakuan.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:57.860
Knock 'em?

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.370
I've heard of this...

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.110
The Uzuurussha take hostages,

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:07.120
and force the people they capture to fight for them.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.870
Which means those are people of Yamato?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.420
Damned cowards!

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:25.770
They shall pay!

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:26.890
I will accompany you.

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.390
Looks like it's time for war.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:33.900
Kokopo!

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:34.770
Wait!

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:47.590
Who's there?

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:48.990
Enemies? Allies?

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.770
The Nakuan are citizens of Yamato.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.670
Don't hurt them!

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.670
I know that!

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.260
Allies?

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.530
Who are they?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.580
Can you really fight?

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:41.610
Who's there?

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.630
Enemies!

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.400
Let's get out of here!

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:53.810
Don't let them escape!

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.410
Don't just stand there!

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.070
Surround them!

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.690
Now this here's an enthusiastic welcome!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.310
We should be safe now.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.230
Don't scare me like that.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.320
Don't worry about it.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.280
Not being able to fight in a war is normal.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:02.570
So the people of Yamato eat this stuff every day?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.050
Look at this stuff!

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:08.050
We're torching the village anyway.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.550
It'd be a waste not to eat what's here.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:15.060
Looks like an Uzuurussha garrison.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.630
They're drinking at this hour? Man, I'm envi—

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.560
I mean, that's terrible.

00:14:33.650 --> 00:14:35.290
Perhaps it was my imagination.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.810
That was close.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.210
Let's get out of here.

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.870
I'm more suited for cleaning ditches, I think.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.230
Move it!

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.050
You found another one?

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:00.080
She was hiding under the floorboards.

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:03.150
Get in!

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.740
Are those the Nakuan hostages you were talking about?

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:13.060
They're pretty well-guarded.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:16.490
They've got them stuffed in a carriage so they can be moved quickly.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.250
Haku-sama...

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:21.750
What is it?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.880
Wait, you're not going to tell me you want to go save them, are you?

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.380
Wait, wait.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.130
Let's go get the others first.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.640
We can't do it on our own.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.140
Haku-sama!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.390
You want to save them?

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:45.900
Can't exactly say no, can I?

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.910
Everyone, you know what to do, right?

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:58.150
Yes!

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.110
Understood.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:00.410
No problem.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.620
If we can break through here, we have a straight path to the capital.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:15.930
I'm counting on you guys.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:30.940
What's that?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.640
Smoke?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:34.970
Fire!

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.570
Someone started the fire already?

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.200
They're in some hurry.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.660
Let's go.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.360
Hurry up!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.450
Fire!

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.210
What's all this noise?

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.210
Put it out!

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.780
It's burning...

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:55.340
What's going to happen to us?

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.720
We're here to save you, everyone!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.220
To save us?

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.740
But Shinonon is still...

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.000
Shinonon?

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.620
Over there, huh?

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.410
Are we gonna be okay?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:14.520
Who goes there?

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.990
We're here to save you!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.620
Who are you?

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:26.600
It doesn't matter.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.120
Let's go.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:29.700
Ow, that's hot!

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:31.880
The smoke is fake?

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:33.560
Explain!

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.920
Entua-sama! The hostages are gone!

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:37.900
What?

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:41.260
Curses!

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.520
Let me go!

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.190
Daddy!

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.940
Stop flailing around, you stupid kid!

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.690
The people of Yamato...

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:58.780
are under our protection!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:17.050
That woman... She took all of them out by herself!?

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.930
You're all that's left!

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:30.730
Sorry, little girl.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:35.320
I can't let you kill him, you know!

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.280
Atui!

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:43.370
What's wrong, little girl?

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.910
I thought you were a little better than this.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.200
Was I imagining it?

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:50.620
He's good.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.750
The way he handles that sword...

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:54.570
That's Yakutowaruto, the Blade Master.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.960
Yakutowaruto?

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:00.410
He appeared at the royal tournament in Yamato three years ago, out of nowhere,

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:04.220
and defeated all challengers to become the de facto winner.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:09.980
The emperor was extremely impressed and offered him fame and a reward.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.810
But the undefeated Blade Master said

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:16.650
it wasn't worth bothering with, and declined.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.880
I-I see...

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.040
Sister,

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.490
there's steam coming out of your head.

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:27.240
I didn't think anyone here would know who I am.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:32.250
Yakutowaruto, we may not look it, 
but we're here to help you!

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:36.740
I don't recall asking for your help.

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:38.200
Kill them now!

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:42.010
Slash them apart and cut off their heads!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.020
You can hate me for this if you want!

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.020
Daddy!

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.420
Shinonon!

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:01.900
What are they doing here?

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.540
Such speed.

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:18.360
So that's Yakutowaruto, the Blade Master.

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:22.920
Daddy!

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.040
Sure am glad everyone's safe and sound.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.310
You got that right.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:44.640
Princess of Kujuuri, you have my gratitude.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:47.450
I am told this was due to your actions.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.000
N-No...

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.370
I just...

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.430
And you too.

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:38.230
Wiped out?

00:22:38.230 --> 00:22:40.520
The Uzuurussha's main force is on the march!

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:43.020
It's only a matter of time before they reach us!

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:49.610
Yamato pissants, know that it is I, Gundurua,

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:51.780
who shall rule the land!

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:54.630
I told you so...

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:56.100
Dekoponpo-sama!

00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:00.300
Hey, you! Do something!

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:04.540
At this point, I don't know what I could possibly do!

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.560
Cease the excuses! You're our tactician!

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:10.310
Do something, you pasty-faced monster!

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:12.050
We're going home.

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:16.310
Dekoponpo-sama?

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:20.310
What!?

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:27.720
Th-The General of the Left and...

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:29.850
the General of the Right...
